ide restart protocol for node1 was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged and observed through connection loss, the post-restart boot identity differed, and system, timer, cleanup behavior, and retained data recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["No naturally elapsed midnight timer firing was captured; the daily outcome is supported by the installed schedule, enabled/active waiting state, manual cleanup behavior, and post-restart recovery.","The controlled age test used six-day-old and eight-day-old files rather than an exactly seven-day-old boundary fixture; the exact threshold is evidenced by the installed -mmin +10079 policy."]}
